                          "text":  "My twin, Pioneer 10, went first and proved the way was open. I launched a year later, in April 1973, and I was sent to do something riskier.\n\nI flew past Jupiter three times closer than my twin had. I dived in fast, to spend as little time as possible in the radiation, and I got the first good look at the top of the planet. Then Jupiter\u0027s gravity flung me up and across the whole solar system, toward a planet no spacecraft had ever visited.",
